# Dotfiles are not assets, and Workers Static Assets — unlike Pages — does not
# exclude them for you. Verified on a throwaway project: /.env and /.DS_Store
# both answered 200 with their contents.
#
# Production builds from a fresh clone, so .gitignore keeps these out of the
# tree there. The gap this closes is a `wrangler deploy` from a workstation
# whose static/ picked up a .DS_Store from Finder — gitignored, therefore
# invisible to `git status` and to review, and published anyway.
**/.??*

# ...except `.well-known/`, which RFC 8615 reserves for exactly the files a
# client fetches by a known URL — security.txt (RFC 9116) lives there. The
# pattern above matches the directory name, so it has to be let back in by name;
# the files inside it are not dotfiles and pass on their own.
!/.well-known
